From f2fae246a19ac1348e76925d637588331d3530ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wangson <wangson@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Dec 2025 19:28:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] arch: arm: cortex_m: initialize LR to 0 to avoid GDB
 backtrace timeout

On ARM Cortex-M, newly created threads may start with
an undefined/garbage LR in the initial exception frame.
When using GDB, the backtrace unwinder can follow this
invalid LR value and end up hanging or timing out while
trying to unwind into a non-existent call chain.
Initialize the LR in the initial interrupt/exception
frame to 0 in arch_new_thread(). Setting LR to 0 acts
as a sentinel for GDB unwinding, indicating the end of
the call chain and preventing backtrace hangs.

Change-Id: Ia3e1ea05571db2f88c7dcbf4ae8455714e8b5e48
---
 arch/arm/core/cortex_m/thread.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/core/cortex_m/thread.c b/arch/arm/core/cortex_m/thread.c
index e7d0f347471..35d4f54ae0a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/core/cortex_m/thread.c
+++ b/arch/arm/core/cortex_m/thread.c
@@ -137,6 +137,8 @@ void arch_new_thread(struct k_thread *thread, k_thread_stack_t *stack, char *sta
 	iframe->a4 = (uint32_t)p3;
 
 	iframe->xpsr = 0x01000000UL; /* clear all, thumb bit is 1, even if RO */
+	/* Initialize LR to 0 to prevent GDB backtrace timeout */
+	iframe->lr = 0;
 
 	thread->callee_saved.psp = (uint32_t)iframe;
 	thread->arch.basepri = 0;
-- 
